{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Every devoted thing in Israel shall be yours.</b> Any person of Israel who devotes (חרם) any of his property without specification — it is forbidden to him and to all Israel, and it belongs to the priests serving in that watch. And in another place it says (Leviticus 27:21–22): ״כשדה החרם לכהן תהיה אחזתו״ — like a devoted field, its holding shall belong to the priest. And if he specified it for Heaven (לשמו יתברך), he gives it to the upkeep of the Temple. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted this in the episode of Korah: there was a certain woman who had a ewe; she came to shear it, and the priest came to her so that she would give him the first of the fleece; when it gave birth to a firstborn, the priest took it; when she saw that things were thus, she slaughtered it; the priest came and took the gifts; she said, 'Let this meat be חרם (devoted)' — he took everything."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:33:47.374781704Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}